          "id": "978e745911f892909b35104e90a5c5e7e35126cd",
          "message": "Add `Fp` to extension field implementation (#2427)\n\nIn our PIL std lib, we have an `Ext` that abstracts over `Fp2` and\n`Fp4`. But in cases where we don't need any extension field (e.g.\nBN254), we wrapped base field elements as `Fp2` anyway. This is a bit\nweird and can lead to issues when the optimizer removes the unused\ndimension (e.g., it might still be referenced by a prover function or\nwitgen annotation). I had this problem in #2426.\n\nNow, there is an `Ext<T>::Fp` variant that simply wraps `T`.",
          "timestamp": "2025-02-03T10:23:50Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/powdr-labs/powdr/commit/978e745911f892909b35104e90a5c5e7e35126cd"
