          "message": "Use in-liner in APC optimizer (#2695)\n\nThis PR has the following changes:\n- In the optimizer, I added a call `replace_constrained_witness_columns`\nand some logging.\n- I removed the rule that a substitution is only executed if the\nsubstituted variable is used, for two reasons:\n- The check was expensive (e.g. on Keccak the in-liner took longer than\nthe solver...)\n- I think it's fair to just remove these identities then. It changes the\nstatement being proven, but the statement is trivial: \"I know some\nvalues that can be computed from other values in the table via a\nlow-degree expression\"\n\nAs seen in https://github.com/powdr-labs/powdr-openvm/pull/108, this\nleads to moderate improvement in the Keccak benchmark.",
