          "id": "12454f5de0c8288d093b366720292bb8a59eb3ac",
          "message": "Add script to update openvm and stark-backend hashes independently (#3469)\n\nAdds a utility script to update openvm or stark-backend git revision\nhashes independently across all Cargo.toml files in the repository.\n\n### Changes\n\n- New `scripts/update-dep.sh` script that:\n- Takes a command argument (\"openvm\" or \"stark-backend\") to specify\nwhich dependency to update\n  - Finds all Cargo.toml files with the specified git dependencies\n  - Updates the `rev = \"...\"` field for all matching entries\n  - Handles paths with spaces and empty results safely\n\n### Usage\n\n```bash\n# Update only openvm dependencies\n./scripts/update-dep.sh openvm v1.5.0-powdr\n\n# Update only stark-backend dependencies\n./scripts/update-dep.sh stark-backend v1.3.0-powdr\n```\n\nThe openvm command updates 17 files: the root `Cargo.toml` (35 openvm\ndeps) and 16 guest Cargo.toml files in `openvm/guest-*/`. The\nstark-backend command updates 1 file: the root `Cargo.toml` (5\nstark-backend deps).\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> Can you make a script to automatically update openvm and stark-backend\nhashes everywhere?\n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n✨ Let Copilot coding agent [set things up for\nyou](https://github.com/powdr-labs/powdr/issues/new?title=✨+Set+up+Copilot+instructions&body=Configure%20instructions%20for%20this%20repository%20as%20documented%20in%20%5BBest%20practices%20for%20Copilot%20coding%20agent%20in%20your%20repository%5D%28https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-tips%29%2E%0A%0A%3COnboard%20this%20repo%3E&assignees=copilot)\n— coding agent works faster and does higher quality work when set up for\nyour repo.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: leonardoalt <504195+leonardoalt@users.noreply.github.com>",
