          "id": "8e725a4e993ec98f238639f5d72f1d871a7d9bd0",
          "message": "Fix mean effectiveness computation (#3585)\n\nBuilds on #3586\n\nThis PR fixes an issue @pacheco found: When calculating mean\neffectiveness, we weight by the cost *before* the optimization. The does\n*not* correspond to the overall reduction in cost; for this, we need to\nweight by the cost *after* the optimization.\n\nRunning the updated code on the most recent reth result leads to\nslightly lower mean effectiveness, compared to the [existing\nplot](https://github.com/powdr-labs/bench-results/blob/gh-pages/results/2026-01-26-0522/reth/effectiveness.png):\n\n<img width=\"3323\" height=\"1768\" alt=\"reth_2026_01_26\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/267d4c31-0ac6-4686-9d85-f95bffd219b9\"\n/>\n\nIf this change is approved, I will also update the [APC\nanalyzer](https://georgwiese.github.io/autoprecompile-analyzer)\naccordingly.",
          "timestamp": "2026-01-27T15:35:08Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/powdr-labs/powdr/commit/8e725a4e993ec98f238639f5d72f1d871a7d9bd0"
