          "id": "872016ee04b4e3b63f74b007bd104d72e544d12f",
          "message": "Generate README for nightly bench-results with links to metrics & APC viewers (#3675)\n\n### Motivation\n- Make published nightly results easier to explore by auto-generating a\n`readme.md` that links each experiment to the hosted OpenVM metrics\nviewer and the APC analyzer.\n- Ensure the README works with different bench-results layouts,\nincluding nested APC runs (e.g. `keccak/apc003/apc_candidates.json`) and\ntop-level APC files (e.g. `reth/apc_candidates.json`).\n\nFor the latest nightly, generates [this\nreadme](https://gist.github.com/georgwiese/cea727e0b24a2efd72a41b2c67321c40).\n\n### Description\n- Add `scripts/generate_bench_results_readme.py`, a small Python helper\nthat scans a `results` directory, detects `combined_metrics.json` and\nthe nearest `apc_candidates.json` per experiment, and emits a Markdown\ntable with viewer links using the GitHub blob paths.\n- The script prefers the shallowest `apc_candidates.json` under each\nexperiment directory so nested run folders (like `apc003/`) are handled\ncorrectly.\n- Wire the generator into `.github/workflows/nightly-tests.yml` for both\nthe CPU and GPU publish jobs so `./results/readme.md` is produced before\nthe step that pushes to the `powdr-labs/bench-results` `gh-pages`\nbranch.\n\n### Testing\n- Compiled the generator with `python3 -m py_compile\nscripts/generate_bench_results_readme.py` and it succeeded.\n- Ran the generator against a synthetic layout with `python3\nscripts/generate_bench_results_readme.py <tmp-results-dir>\n2026-03-18-0537` and inspected the produced output, which contained\nexpected per-experiment links.\n- Verified workflow YAML parses with `ruby -e 'require \"yaml\";\nYAML.load_file(\".github/workflows/nightly-tests.yml\")'` and ran `git\ndiff --check` to ensure no whitespace/errors; both checks succeeded.\n\n------\n[Codex\nTask](https://chatgpt.com/codex/tasks/task_b_69baa02251bc8324b129fba21774e4e6)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
