          "id": "059709502a124465af4b3d5ab8aaaa99d87d48fc",
          "message": "Simplify expressions via exhaustive search on flag variables (#3654)\n\n## Summary\n\n- When the exhaustive search finds multiple valid assignments for flag\nvariables, check if substituting any valid assignment produces the same\nresidual expression. If so, replace the constraint with the simplified\nresidual, eliminating the flag variables.\n- This enables downstream optimizations (e.g., memory alias analysis) to\nrecognize that register addresses are identical when flag-dependent\nsub-expressions always evaluate to the same constant.\n\nExample: if a constraint is `V = X + 4 + f(flags)` and `f(flags)` always\nevaluates to 4 across all valid flag assignments, the constraint is\nsimplified to `V = X + 8`.\n\nCloses #3653\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] All 100 constraint-solver tests pass\n- [x] All 38 autoprecompiles tests pass (including large tests: sha256,\necrecover, optimize)\n- [x] OpenVM tests pass\n- [x] Clippy clean\n- [x] Verify improvement on the `same_register_not_optimized` test case\nfrom womir-openvm\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: chriseth <chriseth.github@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: chriseth <chris@ethereum.org>",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-20T17:54:49Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/powdr-labs/powdr/commit/059709502a124465af4b3d5ab8aaaa99d87d48fc"
