          "message": "ci: split nightly test_apc onto GH-hosted larger runners (#3725)\n\n## From human (Leo)\n\nThis worked well:\n- Nightly run:\nhttps://github.com/powdr-labs/powdr/actions/runs/25311063752\n- guest benches is a lot slower than before now (32 cores vs 48 from our\ndev server), but it runs in parallel to reth\n  - we could consider parallelizing each guest also\n- The first run of the new `publish` job failed because the\n`bench-results` repo (where results are pushed) was too large (14gb).\nThe fix is also in this PR, the code uses a sparse option to only push\nthe new stuff without pulling the entire branch.\n- It then worked:\nhttps://github.com/powdr-labs/powdr/actions/runs/25329189129/job/74258076212\n\n## Summary\n\n- Replace the self-hosted `server-dev` `test_apc` job with two parallel\njobs (`test_apc_guest`, `test_apc_reth`) targeting a new GitHub-hosted\nlarger runner labeled `bench-cpu-128g` (32 vCPU / 128 GiB).\n- Add a `publish_bench_results` job that `needs: [test_apc_guest,\ntest_apc_reth]`, downloads both artifacts, writes `results/run.txt` from\n`$GITHUB_SHA` + the `openvm-eth` ref parsed from\n`.github/actions/patch-openvm-eth/action.yml`, regenerates the readme,\nand does a single `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages` push — no race against\nitself.\n- `bench` (warpbuild) and `test_apc_gpu` (self-hosted GPU) are\nunchanged.\n\n### Why\n\nThe self-hosted `server-dev` runner has been failing nightly since\n~2026-04-29 — last failure was a silent SIGKILL of the reth prover,\ntraced to memory pressure from a stuck restart-looping\n`github-runner.service` (1.4M restarts) plus 56 GiB of stale `/tmp`\nartifacts plus a parallel runner from another user on the same machine.\nMoving CPU nightly to ephemeral GH-hosted runners isolates each run.\n\n### Sizing rationale\n\nPeak RSS from `psrecord.csv` on three recent successful CPU runs\n(2026-04-25/27/28):\n- worst guest bench: ecc-projective at apc030 ≈ 50 GiB\n- reth at apc100 ≈ 32 GiB\n\n128 GiB / 32 vCPU gives ~2.5x headroom on the worst case.\n\n## Pre-merge requirement\n\nThe org needs a runner labeled `bench-cpu-128g` (Ubuntu x64, 32-core/128\nGB SKU) created at **Org Settings → Actions → Runners → New\nGitHub-hosted runner**. Without it, both new jobs will queue forever.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Trigger the workflow via `workflow_dispatch` from this branch and\nverify:\n- [ ] `test_apc_guest` builds, runs `run_guest_benches.sh`, uploads\n`bench-results-guest`\n- [ ] `test_apc_reth` builds, patches openvm-eth, runs all 5 reth APC\nvariants, uploads `bench-results-reth`\n- [ ] `publish_bench_results` downloads both, generates `run.txt` and\n`readme.md`, pushes a single commit to `powdr-labs/bench-results` under\n`results/<date>/`\n- [ ] Resulting bench-results commit matches the layout of prior CPU\nnightly commits (e.g. 2026-04-29-0445)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
