          "id": "a39dca28190e287ae246d687368da2de1c01137a",
          "message": "perf: canonicalize bus mults after add_guards (#3746)\n\nBackground: 95% of the constant folding optimizations in #3740 (2 and 3)\ndone in `emit_expr` for `apc_apply_bus` kernel are due to adding\n`is_valid` to bus interaction multiplicity and constraints.\n\n`add_guards` constructs `is_valid * b.mult` (and `(1 - is_valid) *\nb.mult`) using AlgebraicExpression's overloaded `*`/`-` operators, which\ndo no constant folding — so `is_valid * Number(1)` survives literally\ninto the final SymbolicMachine instead of folding to `is_valid`.\nWrapping each construction in a one-line GroupedExpression roundtrip\ncanonicalizes the result, so every downstream consumer (GPU trace gen,\nCPU prover, debug dumps) sees the canonical form without each having to\nre-implement constant folding.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
